比如，去看哪里增加了复杂度，而不是去查看每一行细节。
Look at, for example, where complexity has been added rather than looking at every line detail specifically.

839
01:09:56,256 --> 01:09:56,656
是的。
Yes.

840
01:09:57,134 --> 01:10:01,668
但我希望达到那种信心水平，即我不再需要去审视代码了。而且我认为这是可行的。
But I want to get to that level of confidence that I don't have to look at the code anymore. And I do think it's possible.

841
01:10:02,176 --> 01:10:02,656
是的。
Yeah.

842
01:10:03,022 --> 01:10:06,980
这也就提出了一个关于测试的好问题。
So it also brings a good point about testing.

843
01:10:09,296 --> 01:10:14,756
而且人们往往容易忽略的一点是，单元测试非常容易造假。
and one of the things that people tend to forget is that a unit test is very fakeable.

844
01:10:15,726 --> 01:10:19,908
所以在单元测试之上还有另一个层面，叫做变异测试。
And so there's a different layer on top of unit testing, and it's called mutation testing.

845
01:10:20,816 --> 01:10:25,216
而变异测试对机器的负担就非常重了。
And mutation testing, on the other hand, is very heavy for your machine.

846
01:10:25,376 --> 01:10:31,376
我之前在给代码做变异测试时，把 CPU 里几个 P 核都搞坏了。
I broke a few P cores in my CPU by doing mutation testing on the code that I was writing.

847
01:10:31,776 --> 01:10:37,536
我认为我们对测试的思考需要再深入一点。
And I think that the way we think about testing needs to go a little bit deeper.

848
01:10:37,776 --> 01:10:46,564
我们需要一些从你建立的脚手架开始，并试图查看有多少比例的脚手架依然稳固的静态代码分析器。
We need to have static code analyzers that start from the scaffold that you did and try to see how much percentage of that scaffold is still standing.

849
01:10:48,176 --> 01:10:50,096
我们需要有办法去
we need to have ways on

850
01:10:51,726 --> 01:10:56,836
拆解每一次提交，看看它是如何推动解决方案前进的。
breaking down each commit and see how it pushed the solution forward.

851
01:10:57,998 --> 01:11:01,856
我认为这可能是个非常好的可视化方式。
And I think that might have a very good way to visualize it.

852
01:11:03,536 --> 01:11:04,932
因为重点不在于
Because it's not about

853
01:11:06,062 --> 01:11:08,896
你从哪开始，到你现在在哪，而是你是怎么走到那里的。
where you start and where you are, but it's how you got there.

854
01:11:10,416 --> 01:11:11,844
我见过很多
I've seen a lot of

855
01:11:13,006 --> 01:11:22,096
智能体犯的错误，就是在迭代几次后它就跟我说：是的，但我之前是那样做的。所以我不知道你要求的是什么。
mistakes by the agent where a few iterations later it just told me, yeah, but I did it like that back there. So I don't know what you're asking.

856
01:11:23,136 --> 01:11:33,216
这些就是我们需要从流程中剔除的部分。因为对我来说，这和被扔进一个全是初级开发者的团队里的过程完全一样。
And those are the parts we need to get out of the process. Because for me, it's exactly the same process as if I were to be thrown into a team with only juniors.

857
01:11:35,182 --> 01:11:38,020
如果我问初级开发者，好吧，祝你好运。
If I ask juniors, okay, have fun.

858
01:11:40,110 --> 01:11:41,216
我会得到代码。
I would get code.

859
01:11:41,966 --> 01:11:46,496
有时甚至能得到很棒的代码，但我得不到一个完整的应用。
I would sometimes even get great code, but I will not get an application.

860
01:11:47,726 --> 01:11:49,936
那么作为资深工程师，你会从哪开始做起？
So as a senior, what do you start doing?

861
01:11:50,096 --> 01:11:55,136
你要开始与产品负责人沟通，让产品规格变得非常清晰。
You start communicating with your PO, getting the product spec absolutely clear.

862
01:11:55,630 --> 01:12:04,496
这就是我与 AI 对话的方式，通过那个图表、那个网络，基本上就是把产品和产品愿景变得非常、非常清晰。
And that's what I do with the conversation with the AI and that graph, that network, is more or less getting the product and the product vision very, very clear.

863
01:12:09,134 --> 01:12:10,052
我来搭建脚手架，
I scaffold,

864
01:12:10,734 --> 01:12:14,020
这是资深工程师在团队中会做的事情。
and that is what a senior engineer would do on a team.

865
01:12:15,216 --> 01:12:20,900
我决定架构，这是资深工程师或架构师会做的事情。
I decide the architecture, that is what a senior engineer or what an architect would do.

866
01:12:21,646 --> 01:12:25,220
我设计我们如何部署这个应用。
I design how we're going to deploy the application.

867
01:12:25,456 --> 01:12:34,896
所以事先我会说，我们要把这个部署到 AWS，或者它需要是一个本地应用，或者你对你要
So beforehand, I would say we're going to deploy this to AWS, or this needs to be a local application, or you set some boundaries on

868
01:12:35,056 --> 01:12:36,176
如何实现这些设定一些边界。
how you want to do that.

869
01:12:36,526 --> 01:12:39,536
你甚至可能还要稍微考虑一下，嗯……
You might even think a little bit about um

870
01:12:41,038 --> 01:12:51,136
如果它要部署到 AWS，你想用哪些应用？你想用 S3 来存储数据吗？你想用 Postgres 数据库吗？还是想用 SQLite？
if it's going to be deployed to AWS. What applications do you want to use? Do you want to use S3 to store your data? Do you want to use a Postgres database? Do you want to use SQLite?

871
01:12:51,376 --> 01:12:56,096
如果你想用 SQLite，你就得有物理文件存储来存放 SQLite 数据库，对吧？
If you want to use SQLite, you need to have some physical file storage to put the SQLite database on, right?

872
01:12:56,176 --> 01:13:06,336
所以你得考虑一下打算怎么部署这个应用，嗯，你想让它怎么运行，以及用户如何与之交互。
So you need to think about how you're going to be deploying the application, uh, how you want it, uh, how you want it running, how you want people interacting with it.

873
01:13:06,510 --> 01:13:14,052
而我觉得，这些决策都不应该让智能体自己去决定。
And then all of that is, I think, something that you do not want to let the agent decide by itself.

874
01:13:16,654 --> 01:13:22,116
因此，在前期就非常清醒地做出这些决策，就是构建脚手架的第一步。
And so being very conscious about those decisions up front is the first phase of scaffolding.

875
01:13:23,776 --> 01:13:26,576
我觉得还有很多东西要学。
I feel like there's still so much to learn.

876
01:13:28,176 --> 01:13:32,496
就像是，既有学习的乐趣，让人兴奋，但也让人感到很有挑战性。
Like both to learn, both that is very exciting, but also very daunting.

877
01:13:32,576 --> 01:13:42,976
每当你意识到这些都是需要在前期完成的工作时，我就在想，这些东西要么是在之前的项目中已经定好了，要么就是我从来没仔细考虑过的。
Like the more you say, this is all the work that you need to do up front. I'm like, man, this is stuff that either in projects has been decided for me or I've never really given it a thought.

878
01:13:43,136 --> 01:13:47,776
我有自己的见解，但我也充满好奇心，迫不及待想去尝试一下了。
I have opinions, but I'm also very curious, and I can't wait to kind of try out.

879
01:13:47,982 --> 01:13:51,536
我觉得我现在比以往任何时候都更想去尝试
I feel like I want to try out now more so than any every any

